# Feature Engineering

The project combines historical time-series information with economically motivated cross-variable features.

## Economic Foundation

The **IS–LM framework** motivates relationships between:

```text
Output
Inflation
Interest Rates
Money Supply
```

This provides theoretical motivation for using lagged cross-variable information.

## Features

The feature set includes:

* Lagged target values
* Cross-variable lags
* Rolling means
* Rolling volatility
* Lagged macroeconomic variables
* Market indicators

## Zero Look-Ahead Bias

All features are constructed using historical information only.

```text
Raw Time Series
      ↓
shift(1)
      ↓
Rolling Statistics
      ↓
Feature Matrix
      ↓
Model
```

Using `.shift(1)` ensures that information from period `t` is not accidentally used to predict the same period.

## Example

```text
GDP(t-1)
   +
CPI(t-1)
   +
Nifty(t-1)
   ↓
Predict GDP(t)
```

This ensures that every prediction is based only on information that would have been available at the forecasting point.

## Small-Sample Considerations

The macroeconomic dataset contains relatively few observations, making:

* Overfitting
* Multicollinearity
* Model variance

important considerations.

This motivates the use of strong regularization and deliberately constrained nonlinear models.
